exports[`supervisor.surface acceptance (as consumer) given: [case2] a verb invoked by name, from a repo with no source when: [t0] \`rhx git.crew.list --help\` is run then: 🔴 and the whole help surface holds its shape 1`] = `
"🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=supervisor/skill=git.crew.list

.what = list every CREW — one line per tree, with the roles that are up

.why  = \`duct.list\` prints one duct per line, so a 26-duct fleet reads
        as 26 rows a human must pair up by eye. but a crew is the unit
        we actually act on: we open a crew, we close a crew, we send a
        crew a message. so it should be the unit we can read.

        it also surfaces a HALF crew at a glance — a tree with only a
        mechanic and no foreman is a supervisor with no way to observe
        without an interrupt of the worker (howto.supervise-routes).

usage:
  rhx git.crew.list

guarantee:
  - read-only: never opens, closes, or sends to any duct
  - derived LIVE from tmux sessions, never from a cached list
  - a one-segment duct (duct:///65 — a human's own shell) is never
    counted as a crew (see term=duct._.choice._.md)
  - exit 0 = listed, 1 = malfunction"
`;

exports[`supervisor.surface acceptance (as consumer) given: [case3] the concurrency verbs, invoked by name from a consumer when: [t0] \`rhx git.crew.tokens --help\` is run then: 🔴 and the whole help surface holds its shape 1`] = `
"🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=supervisor/skill=git.crew.tokens

🌲 git.crew.tokens — each crew's token burn, cost-weighted, on every grove

usage:
  rhx git.crew.tokens                         every grove + local, last 180 min
  rhx git.crew.tokens <grove>                 one grove (or \`local\`)
  rhx git.crew.tokens --window 60             a shorter window, in minutes
  rhx git.crew.tokens --since <iso> --until <iso>
                                              the burn between two utc instants
  rhx git.crew.tokens --json                  one json record in place of the tree, for a tick
  rhx git.crew.tokens calibrate               what 1% of each cap costs, in tokens
  rhx git.crew.tokens calibrate --json        the same, as one json record, for a tick

inputs:
  calibrate          read the cap ledger: weighted tokens per 1% of the 5h and
                     the 7d cap, over every account's reads at once
  <grove> | --grove  a registered grove, or \`local\`        (default: all + local)
  --window           burn window, minutes back from now    (default: 180)
  --since, --until   burn span, two utc instants           (default: the window)
                     the span between them must be 1 min or more
  --span-5h          calibrate: minutes between 5h reads   (default: 120)
  --span-7d          calibrate: minutes between 7d reads   (default: 1440)
  --timeout          seconds per grove                     (default: 90)
  --json             one json record in place of the tree, for a tick

example:
  rhx git.crew.tokens local --window 60"
`;

